  "result": "Excellent! All 87 tests pass (67 original + 20 new discount tests). Here's what I implemented:\n\n\u2705 **Added line discount support** with comprehensive validation\n- `discountPercent` field (0\u2013100, supports decimals like 12.5)\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n- `createInvoice` and `addLine` both accept and validate `discountPercent`\n- Defaults to 0 when not specified\n\n\u2705 **New functions for discount calculations**\n- `lineDiscount(line)` \u2014 calculates discount amount as: lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100\n- Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)` \u2014 now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n  - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals (pre-discount)\n  - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount\n\n\u2705 **Clamping at zero** (house rule)\n- All computed amounts are clamped at 0 using `Math.max(0, ...)`\n- Prevents negative totals even with 100% discounts\n\n\u2705 **Updated rendering** (`renderInvoiceText`)\n- Shows discount amount on each line when applicable: `(12.5% off: -\u20ac42.50)`\n- Shows subtotal and discount lines when there are any discounts\n- All amounts formatted through `formatEuros()`\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests** (20 new) covering:\n- Discount validation (invalid percentages, decimals, 0\u2013100 range)\n- `lineDiscount` calculations (0%, 100%, decimals)\n- `invoiceTotals` with various discount combinations\n- Negative total clamping\n- `addLine` with discounts\n- Rendering with and without discounts",
